---
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader.astro';
import { dataNotice } from '@/lib/api';
import { withBase } from '@/lib/paths';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy notice · draft for owner review"
  description="Temporary note processing, external AI services, browser session storage and deletion limits."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="LEGAL / DRAFT FOR OWNER REVIEW"
    title="What happens to your notes."
    description="The owner must verify service providers, retention and a contact before publishing this as a final notice."
  />
  <Section eyebrow="PRIVACY NOTICE" class="page-section prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        <strong>Draft.</strong> Owner contact pending. Operator identity and
        final service settings have not been supplied.
      </p>
    </div>
    <h2>Before you upload</h2>
    <p>{dataNotice}</p>
    <p>
      You must accept the data notice and complete a security check before a
      live session starts. The check loads after you accept. Files are sent only
      when you choose “Upload queued documents”.
    </p>
    <h2>What stays in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      Selected files and the displayed conversation stay in page memory. They
      are not saved in persistent browser storage. Temporary tab storage saves
      session access, limits, expiry and pending upload progress so a live
      session can resume after reload. The displayed conversation is not
      restored; eligible Intermediate conversation history may remain on the
      server until cleanup.
    </p>
    <h2>Operational records</h2>
    <p>
      Application logs contain operational metadata, not your notes, questions,
      answers, filenames or credentials. Application metadata retention is
      configured for 30 days. Hosting services may keep separate records under
      the owner’s settings.
    </p>
    <h2>Ending a session and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Use “End session” to request deletion of live files, extracted note data
      and conversation history. Session expiry also requests cleanup. Closing a
      tab or clearing browser storage does not immediately delete server data.
      Cleanup can be delayed; provider records and database backups may remain
      longer.
    </p>
    <h2>External services</h2>
    <p>
      Live use involves hosting, security-check, storage and AI service
      providers. They receive the data needed to provide those services. Some
      free AI services may retain prompts or use them for training. The owner
      must confirm the final providers and their terms before live publication.
    </p>
    <p>
      The security-check provider’s{' '}
      <a
        href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        privacy addendum
      </a>{' '}
      explains its processing. Opening the repository link takes you to GitHub.
      Your browser requests the repository's public star count from the GitHub
      API (api.github.com), so GitHub receives that request.
    </p>
    <h2>Local mock mode</h2>
    <p>
      In the labeled local mock, selected file contents are not read, uploaded,
      indexed or sent to a model. Only the file name, type and size are
      validated. No measured timings or answers are simulated. Mock state resets
      on reload.
    </p>
    <h2>Cookies and contact</h2>
    <p>
      No advertising, analytics or session replay is enabled. Read the{' '}
      <a href={withBase('/cookies/')}>storage and cookies draft</a> for
      browser-storage details. Owner contact pending; a real contact is required
      before final publication.
    </p>
  </Section>
</Layout>
